WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.212 --> 00:00:18.622
Sherlock and I continued walking toward our Baker Street lodgings.

2
00:00:19.583 --> 00:00:22.205
"How did you discover where Irene Adler keeps the photograph?"

3
00:00:22.585 --> 00:00:23.005
I asked.

4
00:00:23.025 --> 00:00:26.868
"She showed me just as I said she would," Holmes replied.

5
00:00:26.888 --> 00:00:28.989
"I still don't understand."

6
00:00:29.009 --> 00:00:31.791
"Watson, the matter was perfectly simple."

7
00:00:33.612 --> 00:00:34.552
The detective laughed.

8
00:00:34.572 --> 00:00:38.814
"You saw, of course, that everyone on the street was an accomplice of mine."

9
00:00:39.734 --> 00:00:40.774
"I guessed that was the case."

10
00:00:40.794 --> 00:00:44.655
"When the fight broke out, I had some wet red paint in my palm.

11
00:00:45.696 --> 00:00:50.297
I rushed forward, fell down, and clapped my hand to my face, making it appear that I'd been

12
00:00:50.337 --> 00:00:52.798
wounded." "I also figured that out."

13
00:00:52.818 --> 00:00:56.899
"She was obliged to have me carried into her house," Holmes said.

14
00:00:56.919 --> 00:00:59.900
"And I was taken into her sitting room.

15
00:01:00.952 --> 00:01:03.773
I knew the photograph must be either there or her bedroom."

16
00:01:03.793 --> 00:01:06.395
"But what was the purpose of the smoke bomb?"

17
00:01:06.775 --> 00:01:07.235
I asked.

18
00:01:08.175 --> 00:01:11.957
"When a woman thinks her house is on fire, her instinct is to rush to the thing that

19
00:01:11.997 --> 00:01:14.038
she values most," Holmes explained.

20
00:01:14.058 --> 00:01:19.161
"A married woman runs for her baby; an unmarried one reaches for her jewel box."

21
00:01:20.261 --> 00:01:24.523
Irene Adler rushed to the bellpull, slid back a panel in the wall, and started to remove the

22
00:01:24.563 --> 00:01:26.184
photograph from a secret compartment.

23
00:01:27.148 --> 00:01:31.171
When Holmes announced the false alarm, she replaced the photograph and rushed out of the sitting room.

24
00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:34.294
"I haven't seen her since," said Holmes.

25
00:01:34.314 --> 00:01:38.357
"I was thinking about removing the photograph when her coachman came into the room.

26
00:01:39.998 --> 00:01:42.480
He was watching me carefully, so it seemed safer to wait."

27
00:01:43.441 --> 00:01:44.262
"What happens now?"

28
00:01:44.702 --> 00:01:45.142
I asked.

29
00:01:45.162 --> 00:01:49.006
"Tomorrow morning at eight o'clock we'll go to Briony Lodge with the king.

30
00:01:49.886 --> 00:01:52.268
We will be shown into the sitting room to wait for the lady.

31
00:01:53.129 --> 00:01:56.912
But when she comes downstairs, she probably will not find us or the photograph."

32
00:01:57.792 --> 00:01:59.193
The detective smiled slyly.

33
00:01:59.213 --> 00:02:03.036
"I thought His Majesty might like to recover it with his own hands.

34
00:02:04.116 --> 00:02:05.898
I must send a wire to the king immediately."

35
00:02:06.858 --> 00:02:09.400
At this point we reached Baker Street and stopped at our door.

36
00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:13.843
Holmes was searching his pockets for the key when someone said, "Good night, Mr.

37
00:02:13.883 --> 00:02:19.306
Holmes." There were several people on the sidewalk, but the greeting appeared to come from a slim youth

38
00:02:19.386 --> 00:02:21.748
in a long overcoat, who had hurried past us.

39
00:02:21.768 --> 00:02:27.412
"I've heard that voice before," said Holmes, staring down the dimly lit street.

40
00:02:28.412 --> 00:02:30.413
"Now I wonder who on earth that could have been."

41
00:02:31.353 --> 00:02:35.175
The next morning we were having our toast and coffee when the king of Bohemia rushed into the

42
00:02:35.215 --> 00:02:37.716
room. "You really have the photograph?"

43
00:02:38.037 --> 00:02:41.718
cried the king, grasping Holmes by both shoulders and looking eagerly into his face.

44
00:02:41.738 --> 00:02:44.500
"Not yet," said the detective.

45
00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.501
"But you have hopes of getting it?"

46
00:02:46.861 --> 00:02:47.421
asked the king.

47
00:02:47.441 --> 00:02:49.942
"Yes, I have hopes."

48
00:02:49.962 --> 00:02:53.684
"Then let's get into my carriage and be on our way," said the king.

49
00:02:54.776 --> 00:02:58.777
Once we were settled in the king's carriage, Holmes told him that Irene Adler was married.

50
00:02:58.797 --> 00:03:01.738
"Married! When?

51
00:03:02.158 --> 00:03:02.598
To whom?"

52
00:03:02.618 --> 00:03:05.619
"Yesterday to an English lawyer named Norton."

53
00:03:05.639 --> 00:03:09.320
"But she could not possibly love him," protested the king.

54
00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:12.501
"I hope she does," replied Holmes.

55
00:03:12.521 --> 00:03:16.122
"If the lady loves her husband, then she doesn't love Your Majesty.

56
00:03:17.102 --> 00:03:21.003
And if she doesn't love Your Majesty, then there is no reason she should interfere with your own

57
00:03:21.063 --> 00:03:21.843
plans to marry."

58
00:03:22.824 --> 00:03:23.404
"That's true.

59
00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:25.581
And yet well!

60
00:03:26.542 --> 00:03:28.343
I only wish she had been of my own class.

61
00:03:29.304 --> 00:03:30.444
What a queen she would have made!"

62
00:03:31.305 --> 00:03:35.428
The king fell into a moody silence, which wasn't broken until we arrived at Briony Lodge.

63
00:03:36.369 --> 00:03:39.651
The door of the house was open, and an elderly woman stood upon the steps.

64
00:03:40.672 --> 00:03:44.434
She watched us with a sardonic eye as we alighted from the king's carriage.

65
00:03:46.176 --> 00:03:47.376
"Mr. Sherlock Holmes?"

66
00:03:47.817 --> 00:03:48.277
she said.

67
00:03:48.297 --> 00:03:49.798
"I am Mr.

68
00:03:49.838 --> 00:03:52.200
Holmes," replied my friend, looking rather startled.

69
00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:55.802
"My mistress said you were likely to call," said the woman.

70
00:03:55.822 --> 00:04:00.946
"She left this morning with her husband by the 5:15 train from Charing Cross station.

71
00:04:01.907 --> 00:04:04.248
They were heading somewhere in Europe, never to return."

72
00:04:04.268 --> 00:04:06.090
"The photograph!"

73
00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:07.030
cried the king.

74
00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:08.832
"All is lost."

75
00:04:09.792 --> 00:04:12.875
Holmes pushed past the servant, followed by the king and myself.

76
00:04:13.875 --> 00:04:18.739
He rushed to the bellpull, slid back the wall panel, and, plunging in his hand, pulled out a

77
00:04:18.779 --> 00:04:19.940
photograph and a letter.

78
00:04:20.852 --> 00:04:22.954
The photograph was of Irene Adler alone.

79
00:04:23.835 --> 00:04:25.657
The letter was addressed to Sherlock Holmes.

80
00:04:26.617 --> 00:04:28.819
My friend tore it open and the three of us read it together.

81
00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:34.825
It was dated at midnight and contained the following message: My dear Mr.

82
00:04:34.865 --> 00:04:38.108
Sherlock Holmes: Your disguise fooled me completely.

83
00:04:39.049 --> 00:04:41.551
I was not suspicious until after the cry of fire.

84
00:04:42.412 --> 00:04:46.595
But when I found I had betrayed myself, I remembered that I had been warned about you months

85
00:04:46.636 --> 00:04:51.210
ago. I had been told that if the king employed a detective, it would certainly be you.

86
00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:56.973
Even after I became suspicious, I found it hard to think evil of such a dear old clergyman.

87
00:04:57.873 --> 00:05:01.635
But I have been trained as an actress myself and men's clothes are nothing new to me.

88
00:05:02.596 --> 00:05:05.618
I sent my coachman to watch you while I ran upstairs and changed.

89
00:05:06.598 --> 00:05:10.880
Well, I followed you to your door to be sure I really was an object of interest to

90
00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:11.801
the celebrated Mr.

91
00:05:11.841 --> 00:05:12.641
Sherlock Holmes.

92
00:05:13.682 --> 00:05:17.184
Then I rather imprudently wished you good night and started for my husband's office.

93
00:05:18.124 --> 00:05:22.968
We both thought the best response was to flee, especially when pursued by such a formidable detective.

94
00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.452
As to the photograph, your client may rest in peace.

95
00:05:28.533 --> 00:05:31.535
I love, and am loved by, a better man than he.

96
00:05:32.536 --> 00:05:36.900
The king may do what he likes without interference from the woman whom he has cruelly wronged.

97
00:05:37.841 --> 00:05:42.084
I only keep the photograph as a safeguard against any future actions that he might take.

98
00:05:43.105 --> 00:05:44.686
I leave him another photograph.

99
00:05:45.587 --> 00:05:50.727
Very truly yours, Irene Adler Norton "Oh, what a woman!"

100
00:05:51.107 --> 00:05:51.728
cried the king.

101
00:05:51.748 --> 00:05:54.851
"Didn't I tell you how smart and determined she was?

102
00:05:55.691 --> 00:05:57.553
Wouldn't she have made an admirable queen?

103
00:05:58.554 --> 00:06:00.695
It is a pity that she was not of my own class."

104
00:06:00.715 --> 00:06:05.740
"From what I've seen of the lady, she seems indeed to be in a very different class from

105
00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:07.641
Your Majesty," Holmes said coldly.

106
00:06:07.661 --> 00:06:12.385
"I'm sorry that I haven't been able to bring your case to a more successful conclusion."

107
00:06:12.405 --> 00:06:15.668
"On the contrary," said the king.

108
00:06:16.676 --> 00:06:20.038
"I know that she will keep her word and that the photograph is as safe as if she

109
00:06:20.078 --> 00:06:20.638
had burned it.

110
00:06:21.578 --> 00:06:23.099
Please tell me how I may reward you.

111
00:06:24.059 --> 00:06:28.621
This ring—" He slipped an emerald snake ring from his finger and held it out to Holmes.

112
00:06:28.641 --> 00:06:33.683
"Your Majesty has something that I would value even more highly—that photograph."

113
00:06:33.703 --> 00:06:35.764
"Irene's photograph?"

114
00:06:36.665 --> 00:06:38.145
The king stared at him in amazement.

115
00:06:38.165 --> 00:06:41.046
"Certainly." "Thank you.

116
00:06:41.947 --> 00:06:44.668
Since there is nothing more to be done, I wish Your Majesty good morning."

117
00:06:45.568 --> 00:06:48.109
Holmes bowed, ignoring the hand that the king extended to him.

118
00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:53.592
And that concluded the case where the best plans of the great detective were thwarted by a woman.

119
00:06:54.472 --> 00:06:58.294
Holmes used to make fun of the cleverness of women, but I haven't heard him do that lately.

120
00:06:59.254 --> 00:07:04.397
And when he speaks of Irene Adler, he always refers to her with honor, as the woman.
